# 040 — Product modes (extension)

**Schema:** `argus.mdc.v1` · **Layer:** EXTENSION

## Scope distinction

| Area | Rules |
|------|--------|
| **`argus/`**, **`tests/`**, root `pyproject.toml`** | Full **000–050** |
| **`products/<id>/`** | Product `product.yaml` + user doctrine; do not impose Argus CLI on app runtime without request |

## Rule hierarchy in nested products

Argus MDC (`.cursor/rules/mdc/`) remains the **session-wide** stack (**003**). A product may add **`.cursor/rules/*.mdc` under `products/<id>/`** for subtree-local conventions (imports, venv, git). When both apply to the same edit:

- **000–001** are never overridden by product rules.
- Product rules **override** generic **010** verification *defaults* for that path when documented (**003** conflict clause; **060** onboarding).

## Allowed

- Editing `products/<id>/` when task explicitly names product id.
- Running product-local tests only if documented in that product.

## Disallowed

- Applying Argus portfolio **policy** semantics inside product UI code without user request.
- Deleting product `app/` trees without explicit instruction.

## Failure conditions

- Changing wrong `products/<id>/` vs user intent.

